<div class="ms-bar">
  <button type="button" class="solid-btn" id="admAddUser" data-i18n="adm.addPerson">Add person</button>
</div>

{#- Said before anyone adds somebody and wonders why they cannot sign in.
   Two systems have to agree, and this is only one of them. -#}
<p class="note">
  <b>Adding somebody here does not let them in.</b> They must also exist in
  Cloudflare Access, and their status must be <em>active</em>. Two doors on
  purpose — a mistake on this page grants nothing on its own.
</p>

<form class="ms-form adm-form" id="admUserForm" hidden>
  <div class="ms-grid">
    <label class="fld">
      <span data-i18n="adm.name">Name</span>
      <input type="text" id="admName" maxlength="200" required>
    </label>
    <label class="fld">
      <span data-i18n="adm.email">Email</span>
      <input type="email" id="admEmail" maxlength="200" required>
    </label>
  </div>
  <p class="note-inline" data-i18n="adm.emailNote">
    The email is how Cloudflare Access is matched to this record, so it cannot
    be changed later. Remove and re-invite instead — which leaves a trace.
  </p>
  <div class="ms-actions">
    <button type="submit" class="solid-btn" data-i18n="adm.invite">Invite</button>
    <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" id="admCancel" data-i18n="ms.cancel">Cancel</button>
  </div>
</form>

<div class="adm-people" id="admPeople">
  <p class="empty" data-i18n="common.loading">Loading…</p>
</div>
